/* Only the JNI entry points leave this library. Everything else -- the search,
   the tables, the C API the test binary links statically -- stays internal.
   That is not tidiness: a library loaded into a JVM shares its symbol namespace
   with everything else in the process.

   Both patterns are wildcards on purpose. The NDK links with
   --no-undefined-version --fatal-warnings, which turns naming a symbol the
   library does not define into an error, and this one does not define
   JNI_OnLoad: the entry points are registered by their names, the classic way,
   so there is nothing for it to do. A wildcard that matches nothing is not an
   error, so the pattern can stand ready for the day one is added. */
{
    global:
        Java_dev_skatklar_demo_solve_NativeSolver_*;
        JNI_On*;
    local:
        *;
};
